\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Transport with finitely many sites}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{A field at the head of an edge can be pulled back to its source
by the inverse rotational action. Only finitely many cells enter
the counting pairing. Is finiteness of the rotation group itself
needed for covariance or for the adjoint calculation?}
